We are logging discrepancies where the total sales amount or total USD sales amount differs between your physical summary table and the live Gold view for a specific combination of data source, rollup category, and historical month. The table will also capture "orphaned" records, meaning a specific grouping (like a specific month or category) exists in the view but is entirely missing from the summary table, or vice versa.
​While our new architecture makes mismatches rare, they are absolutely still possible. Because the view always reflects the real-time state of your Silver table, a mismatch will trigger if historical data is updated, deleted, or manually backfilled in the Silver layer, but your summary table's incremental load logic (dl_updated_ts > min_cdc_value) fails to detect and merge those changes during its daily run.
